n style=\\"font-size:10.5pt\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Calibri\\"><span style=\\"font-size:10.5000pt\\"><span style=\\"font-family:宋体\\"><font face=\\"Calibri\\">ll only</font></span></span></span></span><br>"},{"name":"C","content":"<span style=\\"font-size:10.5pt\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Calibri\\"><span style=\\"font-size:10.5000pt\\"><span style=\\"font-family:宋体\\"><font face=\\"Calibri\\">l and ll</font></span></span></span></span><br>"},{"name":"D","content":"<span style=\\"font-size:10.5pt\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Calibri\\"><span style=\\"font-size:10.5000pt\\"><span style=\\"font-family:宋体\\"><font face=\\"Calibri\\">Neither l nor ll</font></span></span></span></span><br>"}],"correct":"<span style=\\"font-size:10.5pt\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Calibri\\"><span style=\\"font-size:10.5000pt\\"><span style=\\"font-family:宋体\\"><font face=\\"Calibri\\">l only</font></span></span></span></span><br>","solution":""},{"type":"choice","article":"<span style=\\"font-size:20px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">The equation&nbsp;<span class=\\"mq-math-mode\\" latex-data=\\"5|x-8|=k\\"><span class=\\"mq-textarea\\"><textarea autocapitalize=\\"off\\" autocomplete=\\"off\\" autocorrect=\\"off\\" contenteditable=\\"false\\" data-cke-editable=\\"1\\" spellcheck=\\"false\\" x-palm-disable-ste-all=\\"true\\"></textarea></span><span class=\\"mq-root-block\\" mathquill-block-id=\\"1\\"><span mathquill-command-id=\\"3\\">5</span><span mathquill-command-id=\\"4\\">|</span><var mathquill-command-id=\\"6\\">x</var><span class=\\"mq-binary-operator\\" mathquill-command-id=\\"7\\">−</span><span mathquill-command-id=\\"8\\">8</span><span mathquill-command-id=\\"9\\">|</span><span class=\\"mq-binary-operator\\" mathquill-command-id=\\"11\\">=</span><var mathquill-command-id=\\"12\\">k</var></span></span>&nbsp;, where <em>k</em> is a constant, has exactly one solution. Which&nbsp;of the following could be the value of&nbsp;<span class=\\"mq-math-mode\\" latex-data=\\"\\\\frac{k}{5}\\"><span class=\\"mq-textarea\\"><textarea autocapitalize=\\"off\\" autocomplete=\\"off\\" autocorrect=\\"off\\" contenteditable=\\"false\\" data-cke-editable=\\"1\\" spellcheck=\\"false\\" x-palm-disable-ste-all=\\"true\\"></textarea></span><span class=\\"mq-root-block\\" mathquill-block-id=\\"1\\"><span class=\\"mq-fraction mq-non-leaf\\" mathquill-command-id=\\"13\\"><span class=\\"mq-numerator\\" mathquill-block-id=\\"14\\"><var mathquill-command-id=\\"18\\">k</var></span><span class=\\"mq-denominator\\" mathquill-block-id=\\"15\\"><span mathquill-command-id=\\"19\\">5</span></span><span style=\\"display:inline-block;width:0\\">​</span></span></span></span>&nbsp;?&nbsp;</span></span><br>","question":"","options":[{"name":"A","content":"-8 or 8<br>"},{"name":"B","content":"-8 only&nbsp;<br>"},{"name":"C","content":"0 only<br>"},{"name":"D","content":"8&nbsp;only<br>"}],"correct":"0 only<br>","solution":""},{"type":"choice","article":"<span style=\\"font-size:20px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\"><img height=\\"246\\" src=\\"/images/9fdb2a27a6849a30f2bea07208ec1d38.png\\" width=\\"768\\"><br>The table shows the frequencies of the values for data set A and data set B, where <i><span style=\\"font-style:italic\\">n</span></i>&nbsp;is a positive&nbsp;integer constant. Which of the following statements best compares the means of the two data&nbsp;sets?</span></span><br>","question":"","options":[{"name":"A","content":"<span style=\\"font-size:20px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">The mean of data set A is greater than the mean of data set B.</span></span><br>"},{"name":"B","content":"<span style=\\"font-size:20px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">The mean of data set A is less than the mean of data set B.</span></span><br>"},{"name":"C","content":"<span style=\\"font-size:20px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">The mean of data set A is equal to the mean of data set B.</span></span><br>"},{"name":"D","content":"<span style=\\"font-size:20px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">There is not enough information to compare the means of the two data sets.</span></span><br>"}],"correct":"<span style=\\"font-size:20px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">The mean of data set A is less than the mean of data set B.</span></span><br>","solution":""},{"type":"write","article":"<span style=\\"font-size:20px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">The quadratic function g models the depth, in meters, below the surface of the water of a Weddell seal t minutes after the seal entered the water during a dive. The function estimates that the seal reached its maximum depth of 382.2 meters 7 minutes after it entered the water and then reached the surface of the water 14 minutes after it entered the water. Based on the function, what was the estimated depth, to the nearest meter, of the seal 10 minutes after it entered the water?</span></span><br>","question":"","options":[],"correct":"312","solution":""},{"type":"choice","article":"<span class=\\"mq-math-mode\\" latex-data=\\"f\\\\left(x\\\\right)=11x^{10}+3x^8\\\\ \\\\ g\\\\left(x\\\\right)=-17x^7+9x^5\\"><span class=\\"mq-textarea\\"><textarea autocapitalize=\\"off\\" autocomplete=\\"off\\" autocorrect=\\"off\\" contenteditable=\\"false\\" data-cke-editable=\\"1\\" spellcheck=\\"false\\" x-palm-disable-ste-all=\\"true\\"></textarea></span><span class=\\"mq-root-block\\" mathquill-block-id=\\"1\\"><var class=\\"mq-f\\" mathquill-command-id=\\"12\\">f</var><span class=\\"mq-non-leaf\\" mathquill-command-id=\\"13\\"><span class=\\"mq-scaled mq-paren\\" style=\\"transform: scale(1, 1.2);\\">(</span><span class=\\"mq-non-leaf\\" mathquill-block-id=\\"14\\"><var mathquill-command-id=\\"16\\">x</var></span><span class=\\"mq-scaled mq-paren\\" style=\\"transform: scale(1, 1.